
# The corpus is committed as a byte artifact, not as text.
#
# Every real profile is CRLF and the formatter branches on that — it detects the
# file's line ending and writes back whichever it found. Left to git, these would
# be stored as LF and checked out as LF on a Linux runner, so the check whose
# whole contract is "a save never alters what FS Copilot loads" would be running
# against files git had rewritten. See docs/pipeline/03-checks.md.
corpus/profiles/** -text
corpus/formatted/** -text
